{"name":"Caneel Bay","hex":"#009bb3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Batuley."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.","A bank or dam to keep back water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caneel Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Caneel Bay was a resort set on a 170-acre peninsula in the Virgin Islands National Park. The resort, near picturesque beaches, is a vacation destination in the Caribbean. It is located on the northwest side of St. John, US Virgin Islands. The resort is within Virgin Islands National Park, on property once owned by Laurance Rockefeller, and operates under a unique agreement with the US National Park Service. The RUE agreement enables the resort to operate with a unique tax-free, rent-free status since 2004."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Caneel_Bay_Boat_Mary_II_at_Caneel_Beach.jpg/330px-Caneel_Bay_Boat_Mary_II_at_Caneel_Beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caneel_Bay","wikidata":"Q5032242"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Peter_Duurloo_%281756-1795%29.jpg/250px-Peter_Duurloo_%281756-1795%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6e/Peter_Duurloo_%281756-1795%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Peter_Duurloo_%281756-1795%29.jpg/250px-Peter_Duurloo_%281756-1795%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Peter Duurloo (1756–1795)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APeter_Duurloo_(1756-1795).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Caneel_Bay_Sunset_by_Cottage_7.jpg/120px-Caneel_Bay_Sunset_by_Cottage_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Caneel_Bay_Sunset_by_Cottage_7.jpg/250px-Caneel_Bay_Sunset_by_Cottage_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Caneel_Bay_Sunset_by_Cottage_7.jpg/120px-Caneel_Bay_Sunset_by_Cottage_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"http